<title>ITALY: Italian CPI 2.6 pct in January - Istat.</title>
<headline>Italian CPI 2.6 pct in January - Istat.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Statistics Office (ISTAT) reported the following consumer inflation details:</p>
<p> ITALIAN INFLATION	   Jan 97     Dec 96     Jan 96</p>
<p> Monthly CPI index rise	 0.2	 0.1	 0.1</p>
<p> Yr-on-yr inflation	     2.6	 2.6	 5.5</p>
<p> Index (Base 1996)	    105.1     104.9     102.4</p>
<p>Istat said that including tobacco costs in the inflation data gave a CPI rate of 2.6 percent for January.</p>
<p>ISTAT gave the following sector-by-sector breakdown.</p>
<p> Sector			   Index	   mo/mo (%)    yr/yr (%)</p>
<p> Food (without tabacco)	104.5	  -0.1	   2.2</p>
<p> Clothing			  105.9	   0.0	   3.3</p>
<p> Housing,Electricity,Fuel    108.2	   1.1	   5.0</p>
<p> Domestic goods		  104.8	   0.0	   2.4</p>
<p> Health spending		 105.0	   2.2	   2.9</p>
<p> Transport			 105.4	  -0.5	   2.7</p>
<p> Recreation			103.6	  -0.1	   1.6</p>
<p> Education			 107.2	   0.0	   3.9</p>
<p> Hotels, restaurants	   105.4	   0.5	   3.1</p>
<p> Other goods,services	  103.1	   0.0	   1.0</p>
<p>(including communications)</p>
</text>
